\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.7}{\ignorespaces The top panel shows the power that was incident on the PMC and the power emerging from the PMC over a 55 hour trail run. The light produced by the amplifiers did not change significantly for the duration of this measurement, however the transmitted light through the PMC dropped from 111\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\watt } to, at its lowest, 107\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\watt }. This is likely due to the environmental conditions in the lab changing. The bottom panel shows the humidity of the lab. Changes in the humidity, which can be caused by a temperature change, coincide with changes in the power emerging from the PMC.\relax }}{25}{figure.caption.22}}
\newlabel{fig:ligolaserchapterpowerplot}{{4.7}{25}{The top panel shows the power that was incident on the PMC and the power emerging from the PMC over a 55 hour trail run. The light produced by the amplifiers did not change significantly for the duration of this measurement, however the transmitted light through the PMC dropped from 111\,\si {\watt } to, at its lowest, 107\,\si {\watt }. This is likely due to the environmental conditions in the lab changing. The bottom panel shows the humidity of the lab. Changes in the humidity, which can be caused by a temperature change, coincide with changes in the power emerging from the PMC.\relax }{figure.caption.22}{}}
