\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.9}{\ignorespaces The top panel shows that as the second amplifier head's temperature increases the power produced by it decreases. The bottom panel shows that the higher order mode content increases as the temperature of the amplifier increases. This means that the power in the fundamental mode decreases as the temperature decreases due to two effects: less overall power and worse beam quality.\relax }}{29}{figure.caption.30}}
\newlabel{fig:ligo_laser_chapter_cooling_pwoer_hom}{{4.9}{29}{The top panel shows that as the second amplifier head's temperature increases the power produced by it decreases. The bottom panel shows that the higher order mode content increases as the temperature of the amplifier increases. This means that the power in the fundamental mode decreases as the temperature decreases due to two effects: less overall power and worse beam quality.\relax }{figure.caption.30}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.10}{\ignorespaces Mode scans were performed with the DBB for each amplifier head temperature. The second order mode for this cavity is located at $\sim 0.3$ FSR; its exact location drifts due to thermal expansion of the cavity. As the temperature of the amplifier head changes, the second order mode content of the beam changes at the percent level. This second order mode height is shown in the inset. The second order mode changes due to the beam's astigmatism changing.\relax }}{30}{figure.caption.31}}
\newlabel{fig:ligolaserchaptermodescans}{{4.10}{30}{Mode scans were performed with the DBB for each amplifier head temperature. The second order mode for this cavity is located at $\sim 0.3$ FSR; its exact location drifts due to thermal expansion of the cavity. As the temperature of the amplifier head changes, the second order mode content of the beam changes at the percent level. This second order mode height is shown in the inset. The second order mode changes due to the beam's astigmatism changing.\relax }{figure.caption.31}{}}
